{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice","id":161194,"title":"Idigam Weekly Discussion-Storm Lords(Bones of Ice)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-06T15:44:07-07:00","id":161194,"title":"Idigam Weekly Discussion-Storm Lords(Bones of Ice)","content":"We didn't get a full thing, but we <i>did </i>get a write up on the Storm Lords. <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/bones-of-ice/\" target=\"_blank\">It's pretty cool.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T15:45:27-07:00","id":161204,"title":"","content":"Reposted from the comments:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Personally, I\u2019m still not seeing the connection. Some great material in there, no doubt, but for me it didn\u2019t really shed any more light on why the Storm Lords in particular would view the Spirit-Ridden as the deadliest prey. I mean, it kinda said that they mock spirit and flesh, and that it\u2019s especially offensive to the Uratha, since they\u2019re spirit-hybrids themselves\u2026 But I didn\u2019t really see any particular reason why that would make the Storm Lords want to hunt them or consider them the most dangerous prey any more than it would the other Tribes.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T15:50:12-07:00","id":161230,"title":"","content":"You'll note the section about how the Iminir see themselves as the heirs to Father/Mother Wolf, and the Spirit-Ridden are the most blatant insult to the Great Wolf's duty - they exemplify everything that is a transgression of the boundary that Ur-Farah guarded. That's really important to the Storm Lords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T15:54:26-07:00","id":161232,"title":"","content":"Also, FOR NO REASON WHATSOEVER, is it ok if I throw out a request into this thread for opinions about Rites? Any thoughts from people about bits or elements of the old Rites systems that you really liked or hated? Not just the stuff in the corebook, but were there any particular developments in how Rites were handled in later books that you thought were good or need to be steered away from?<br /> <br /> Just... assessing opinions.<br /> <br /> No reason. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T16:02:40-07:00","id":161234,"title":"","content":"The outright binding, summoning and so forth of spirits was a pretty big pull for me. I know some people don't like the spirit, but I certainly did. I do think they could use some more limitations than dice rolls. Summoning I could see at a penalty if you didn't know the spirit you were targeting, but it makes sense to require more for binding a spirit to a place or object. Obviously creating fetishes was a really cool aspect of it.<br /> <br /> There were a few rites that really bugged me. One of them was banish human, which you could do to kick someone out of the Shadow, but it only worked on absolutely normal humans, which was the kind of 'so limited it may as well be useless' kind of thing that annoyed me about Werewolf. And as a point to the binding spirit thing, it feels like the writers were trying to be very careful when writing it so as to not make the rituals seem too powerful, resulting in many of them being weak and/or useless. One should be able to bind spirits to more than just places (like people, or objects without necessarily making a fetish).<br /> <br /> Plus things like rites that offer no mechanical benefit. It know what they mean, and the intent is appreciated, but you only have so much experiences to throw around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-06-2014, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T16:16:05-07:00","id":161239,"title":"","content":"Can someone please tell me I'm not alone in not liking the &quot;Tribe as fixated on specific prey&quot; thing Idigam Chronicles seems to be running with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T16:20:01-07:00","id":161242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161239#post161239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone please tell me I'm not alone in not liking the &quot;Tribe as fixated on specific prey&quot; thing Idigam Chronicles seems to be running with.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I <i>can</i> tell you you're making a fixation out of a specialty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T16:26:47-07:00","id":161246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161232#post161232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, FOR NO REASON WHATSOEVER, is it ok if I throw out a request into this thread for opinions about Rites? Any thoughts from people about bits or elements of the old Rites systems that you really liked or hated? Not just the stuff in the corebook, but were there any particular developments in how Rites were handled in later books that you thought were good or need to be steered away from?<br /> <br /> Just... assessing opinions.<br /> <br /> No reason. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I found the idea that a dedicated prepared ritual space could alleviate some of the penalties rituals take (like the Iron Masters' private space in Tribes of the Moon allowing a ritualist to ignore penalties for urban areas) to be an interesting notion.<br /> <br /> Also, I enjoyed the concept of rites as things that powerful spirits are good for teaching/making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-06-2014, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T16:58:32-07:00","id":161273,"title":"","content":"Aisha! I'm VIBRATING!<br /> <br /> Werewolves getting some Slasher vibes, love it more every time I see it. Really eager to see the other tribes now. Dig the Sin-eater stereotype, too, bout time some splats had some motive to go after one another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ExLqMBLyWd8\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ExLqMBLyWd8\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ExLqMBLyWd8\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ExLqMBLyWd8 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-06-2014, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T17:11:29-07:00","id":161280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Sin-Eaters:</b> Claimed by the dead is still Claimed. </div> </div> </div>*_* fantastic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T20:08:27-07:00","id":161367,"title":"","content":"You know what actually made the Ridden thing make sense to me? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even when not hunting the Claimed, Storm Lords know the warning signs to look for:<br /> <br /> the weak-willed, the isolated, the vulnerable, the kinds of people who need something <br /> <br /> to fill that hollow place inside them are prime fodder for possession. </div> </div> </div>For a tribe that swore an oath to show no weakness, this actually makes a lot of sense to me. Those who would show weakness are putting a big &quot;possess me!&quot; sign on them. If the Storm Lords are to keep the Claimed at bay, they can afford themselves no such luxury.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T21:17:05-07:00","id":161394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>underwoodfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161367#post161367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a tribe that swore an oath to show no weakness, this actually makes a lot of sense to me. Those who would show weakness are putting a big &quot;possess me!&quot; sign on them. If the Storm Lords are to keep the Claimed at bay, they can afford themselves no such luxury.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda see the cause and effect reversed. The Claimed are the ultimate example of what happens when you show too much weakness. They're the most dangerous prey less because they're capable of doing bad things and more because they're the danger of weakness itself made manifest.<br /> <br /> That kind of construction doesn't work for the other tribes, but it does here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T21:47:36-07:00","id":161407,"title":"","content":"Oh, I like that! I wish that had been expanded on a little more in the writeup, cause that's a really cool explanation of why they would see them as the most dangerous prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T22:24:08-07:00","id":161421,"title":"","content":"I have very obvious question, but that is crucial to this sticking Tribes with they favorite Prey \u2013 what is if I don\u2019t want to use specific kind of threat in chronicle? For example, I now run game based on Bale Hounds and Malejin threat. I have little, secluded town in far reaches of Sweden. Using spoilers of Idigam Chronicles as written, sure, I will have Blood Talons for Bale Hounds, Storm Lords for Spirit-Ridden taken by Malinets demons, and Iron Masters for fighting with humans cult that worship Malejin. But this little town on the outskirts of civilization is also great place for Hunters in Darkness and I don\u2019t see a place for them in chronicle structure and I don\u2019t want to push them on force in to story. What to do in this case? Adding next threat in the overcrowded game isn\u2019t solution for this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, were is gender swapping on Father/Mother Wolf and Mother Luna/ Father Moon now? It\u2019s a bit crucial in mythological part of my Sweden game, as I imagined that local Uratha think they are children of Angerboda, Mother of Wolves and Mani, Father Moon. It has sense, isn't it?<br /> <br /> And last but not least - with all write-up of WInter Wolf, there is a lot more sense of my little town to be in everlasting ( for time of chronicle <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) grip of snow. Had Skolis-Ur appeared in the area to test young Wolf-Blooded? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T22:37:17-07:00","id":161424,"title":"","content":"Using the Storm Lords as an example, there is still a place for the implacable oncoming storm in most stories, and Tribes aren't just their favored prey. Their favored prey sharpens the understanding of them, but it doesn't define them. What still comes first are things like the tribe bans, their renown, and general tribal attitudes.<br /> <br /> <br /> So for the Storm Lords, just because the Claimed aren't here doesn't mean the pack doesn't need someone who will never back down, who will always inspire the others to keep standing, and to bring down the powers of the sky upon them. For the Hunters in Darkness, just because the shartha aren't there doesn't mean that a pack doesn't need a sneaky bastard with a mind for purity of purpose and place.<br /> <br /> We've been over this: <b><i><u>PREY IS NOT THE END ALL, BE ALL OF THE TRIBES.</u></i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T22:48:54-07:00","id":161428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161421#post161421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have very obvious question, but that is crucial to this sticking Tribes with they favorite Prey \u2013 what is if I don\u2019t want to use specific kind of threat in chronicle? For example, I now run game based on Bale Hounds and Malejin threat. I have little, secluded town in far reaches of Sweden. Using spoilers of Idigam Chronicles as written, sure, I will have Blood Talons for Bale Hounds, Storm Lords for Spirit-Ridden taken by Malinets demons, and Iron Masters for fighting with humans cult that worship Malejin. But this little town on the outskirts of civilization is also great place for Hunters in Darkness and I don\u2019t see a place for them in chronicle structure and I don\u2019t want to push them on force in to story. What to do in this case? Adding next threat in the overcrowded game isn\u2019t solution for this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of people are taking the favored prey thing to be a bit more significant than it actually is. Like Satchel said, it's not a fixation, it's a specialty. Just because there are no Hosts around doesn't mean the Hunters in Darkness have nothing to do but sit on their hands and wait for some Azlu to show up. A Tribe considers it's favored prey to be the most dangerous, and therefore the most worthy. But just because hamburgers are my favored lunch and I consider them to be the tastiest, and therefore most worthy does not mean I won't eat a salad from time to time. Likewise, a Hunter in Darkness would still be perfectly willing and able to help the pack fight a Bale Hound threat. In fact, they would have a unique perspective on that threat not shared by members of other Tribes who have different priorities in terms of prey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161421#post161421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, were is gender swapping on Father/Mother Wolf and Mother Luna/ Father Moon now? It\u2019s a bit crucial in mythological part of my Sweden game, as I imagined that local Uratha think they are children of Angerboda, Mother of Wolves and Mani, Father Moon. It has sense, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gender pronouns are fairly meaningless to spirits, especially ones as powerful and abstract as Urfarah and Luna. I'm not familiar with the Angerboda or Mani you're referring to, but I assume they are Sweedish mythological figures that parallel Luna and Urfarah? That's a great example of the reason for the new ambiguous approach. There are probably a great deal of mythological figures from around the world that bare similar resemblance to them, and there are undoubtedly some that are male, some that are female, and some that are both or neither. In the World of Darkness, those myths were most likely influenced by the spirits themselves, and probably influenced the spirits in turn. So sometimes you'll see Luna referred to as Mother, and other times as Father, and likewise for Urfarah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161421#post161421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And last but not least - with all write-up of WInter Wolf, there is a lot more sense of my little town to be in everlasting ( for time of chronicle <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) grip of snow. Had Skolis-Ur appeared in the area to test young Wolf-Blooded? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is super cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T23:01:17-07:00","id":161432,"title":"","content":"Satchel and I are one now?<br /> <br /> I can dig it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T23:19:59-07:00","id":161443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161428#post161428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gender pronouns are fairly meaningless to spirits, especially ones as powerful and abstract as Urfarah and Luna. I'm not familiar with the Angerboda or Mani you're referring to, but I assume they are Sweedish mythological figures that parallel Luna and Urfarah? That's a great example of the reason for the new ambiguous approach. There are probably a great deal of mythological figures from around the world that bare similar resemblance to them, and there are undoubtedly some that are male, some that are female, and some that are both or neither. In the World of Darkness, those myths were most likely influenced by the spirits themselves, and probably influenced the spirits in turn. So sometimes you'll see Luna referred to as Mother, and other times as Father, and likewise for Urfarah.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more pointing out that Stew promised to change Father Wolf with Mother Wolf, from time to time. Now we see a first draft and all it say's is Father Wolf, no Mother. With this, I started to question is maybe devs changed they mind and stick to old paradigm - which would be far worse. Like I mentioned in previous post - I like idea that I can tweak a bit Uratha culture to local taste and in Scandinavia with it's myths more logical is Mother of Wolves pairing with Father Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T23:53:09-07:00","id":161457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161432#post161432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel and I are one now?<br /> <br /> I can dig it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, when I said<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161428#post161428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Satchel said, it's not a fixation, it's a specialty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161242#post161242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but I <i>can</i> tell you you're making a fixation out of a specialty.</div> </div> </div> </div>but I can see how that would have been confusing, since your post immediately preceding mine did say<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161424#post161424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i><u>PREY IS NOT THE END ALL, BE ALL OF THE TRIBES.</u></i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T00:04:36-07:00","id":161458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161232#post161232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, FOR NO REASON WHATSOEVER, is it ok if I throw out a request into this thread for opinions about Rites? Any thoughts from people about bits or elements of the old Rites systems that you really liked or hated? Not just the stuff in the corebook, but were there any particular developments in how Rites were handled in later books that you thought were good or need to be steered away from?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of rites as pieces of magic that transform locations into horror settings, as put forth by Ethan Skemp, is pretty great; I'd like to see more emphasis on it.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see rites that give packs abilities that are essential for hunting treated as standard abilities that all werewolves possess instead of rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T00:18:20-07:00","id":161463,"title":"","content":"I like how the very first &quot;this story is true&quot; piece of mythology isn't compatible with the &quot;Skolis-Ur is the second-oldest of the Firstborn&quot; thing that the Iminir believe.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Even when not hunting the Claimed, Storm Lords know the warning signs to look for: the weak-willed, the isolated, the vulnerable, the kinds of people who need something to fill that hollow place inside them are prime fodder for possession. Storm Lords are experts at finding those people in their prey\u2019s orbit. They can smell the need, and they have no compunction about using it.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Problematic, but appropriately so for a horror game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T01:39:03-07:00","id":161492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161232#post161232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, FOR NO REASON WHATSOEVER, is it ok if I throw out a request into this thread for opinions about Rites? Any thoughts from people about bits or elements of the old Rites systems that you really liked or hated? Not just the stuff in the corebook, but were there any particular developments in how Rites were handled in later books that you thought were good or need to be steered away from?<br /> <br /> Just... assessing opinions.<br /> <br /> No reason. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you want my opinion on Rites, I enjoyed them, but hated Rite of Dedication with a passion bordering on insanity. I felt that anytime you had a ritual that played fast and loose with the rules in addition to being almost 100% mandatory for any Werewolf regardless of playstyle, then you have an issue. The primary issue was that this ritual alone let Werewolves take items to the Shadow which was extremely powerful in addition to being the only ritual that let Werewolves not become naked every 20 minutes. However, all of that pales in comparison to the built in mechanic to bypass the Primal Urge limit through exceptional successes and the ability to dedicate an entire bag worth of items for the same cost. Why would I dedicate a gun when I could dedicate an entire bag worth of guns for the same price? That, and if I played the system long enough, I can gain an exceptional success and dedicate even more issues.<br /> <br /> Long story short? I like rites, but that ritual needs to go or be heavily reworked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T03:13:28-07:00","id":161539,"title":"","content":"So a lot of people are complaining about the prey focus - I am not. But I have to say that I didn't really feel the Claimed as the Storm Lord's primary foe. Nothing about the Claimed, or at least the write up here, seemed to encourage or tie into the core theme of Endurance. Hunting a Claimed doesn't require or encourage Endurance on a werewolf's part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T03:27:57-07:00","id":161545,"title":"","content":"My favourite tribe out of the five, and I feel its better than ever. What originallt drove me to like the Storm Lords, when they at first seemed like a Silver Fang and Shadow Lord combo, was the Tribe's of the Moon description of 'defiance'. It's not just that they will not stop their hunt, but also that they do not want to give their enemy the pleasure of killing them in its own terms.<br /> <br /> I like the way they test each other, and the cultural note (always important, in my opinion) on those who live in warmer climates reaching for Skolis-Ur. The meeting to see each other's weakness as well really works.<br /> <br /> But most I like the visible cultural shift. Now, the Storm Lords aren't the tribe who lead because of Skolis-Ur's mistake. They lead, because they are often the most toughest bastards around and it impresses other uratha. That, and the fact that they themselves don't see themselves as the leader tribe, just trying to fill a role well.<br /> <br /> The replacing Father Wolf part is also nice, the spirit is dead, and he fell to Weakness. So it is up to the Storm tribe to fill his shoes and do his role. I feel this changes things in an interesting way, as the angst factor is gone and duty is more present.<br /> <br /> As for the hints of the Pure, the nickname is interesting and I wonder if it refers to 'bringing the winter' as in the story provided. But more than that, in older Forsaken stories, the Pure first-born were included(If I remember right). Now, it seems only the Forsaken are involved. Might be that the Forsaken are excising the Pure from their mythos on purpose. Or might be the role of the Pure has changed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T03:40:19-07:00","id":161546,"title":"","content":"I just want to point out the bit about werewolves in Bangkok locking themselves in refrigerated trucks for the glory of their tribe. I'm sorry, but I hate that - it's a bizarrely northern-hemisphere centric bit that jettisons local cultural ideas for a very specific interpretation of 'winter' which is bound in ice and snow. Either you have it be about winter and harsh conditions around the world, or you on't bring in other world ideas and shoehorn them into metaphysical niches. Their <i>Storm</i> Lords, not Ice Lords","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T05:42:12-07:00","id":161595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161539#post161539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a lot of people are complaining about the prey focus - I am not. But I have to say that I didn't really feel the Claimed as the Storm Lord's primary foe. Nothing about the Claimed, or at least the write up here, seemed to encourage or tie into the core theme of Endurance. Hunting a Claimed doesn't require or encourage Endurance on a werewolf's part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they don't, actually. They tie into the fact that Storm Lords take the idea that they're Ufarah's descendants the most literally and seriously - &quot;keep separate the children of two worlds.&quot; Spirit-Claimed are, by definition, the exact opposite of that, a fusion between two of the children into something unnatural.<br /> <br /> You <i>do </i>have to be able to Endure to hunt them, though - every Claimed is a race of one, with unique abilities and weaknesses. And learn what that is in a timeframe that leads to less deaths and destruction, perhaps even get it in the window of time it's vulnerable to exorcism and save the human half, you need to experience it firsthand. As subject.<br /> <br /> Then you can start getting a handle on weaknesses...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T05:45:36-07:00","id":161596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161539#post161539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunting a Claimed doesn't require or encourage Endurance on a werewolf's part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't imagine how one would come to this conclusion after having read the Ridden chapter of Predators.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161545#post161545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But most I like the visible cultural shift. Now, the Storm Lords aren't the tribe who lead because of Skolis-Ur's mistake. They lead, because they are often the most toughest bastards around and it impresses other uratha. That, and the fact that they themselves don't see themselves as the leader tribe, just trying to fill a role well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really a change in focus and/or something new. Like, at all. These elements have been part of the Iminir ever since the corebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161545#post161545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the hints of the Pure, the nickname is interesting and I wonder if it refers to 'bringing the winter' as in the story provided. But more than that, in older Forsaken stories, the Pure first-born were included(If I remember right). Now, it seems only the Forsaken are involved. Might be that the Forsaken are excising the Pure from their mythos on purpose. Or might be the role of the Pure has changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't see the basic role of the Pure, that of being implacable enemies who provide the other side of the werewolf experience - that of being hunted - changing in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 06-07-2014, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T06:06:30-07:00","id":161601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161595#post161595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You <i>do </i>have to be able to Endure to hunt them, though - every Claimed is a race of one, with unique abilities and weaknesses. And learn what that is in a timeframe that leads to less deaths and destruction, perhaps even get it in the window of time it's vulnerable to exorcism and save the human half, you need to experience it firsthand. As subject.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your argument is that you need to learn and move quickly? What does that have to do with Endurance?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161596#post161596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't imagine how one would come to this conclusion after having read the Ridden chapter of Predators.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's not actually an argument.<br /> <br /> (P.S. your second quote tag is wrong)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T06:19:16-07:00","id":161609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161280#post161280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *_* fantastic</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I imagine they'd see Changelings roughly the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T06:20:44-07:00","id":161610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161239#post161239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone please tell me I'm not alone in not liking the &quot;Tribe as fixated on specific prey&quot; thing Idigam Chronicles seems to be running with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's better than the &quot;vague spiritual alignment with no real cultural context&quot; we had before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T06:33:48-07:00","id":161618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161601#post161601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's not actually an argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not, it's a rejection of the premise of your argument - if you don't know how hunting creatures that hide in the souls of people, that you can't see, requires endurance, then you don't know Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Also, I think people should stop using &quot;Claimed&quot; when they actually mean &quot;Ridden&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161601#post161601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(P.S. your second quote tag is wrong)</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake, sorry about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T06:39:07-07:00","id":161623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161232#post161232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, FOR NO REASON WHATSOEVER, is it ok if I throw out a request into this thread for opinions about Rites? Any thoughts from people about bits or elements of the old Rites systems that you really liked or hated? Not just the stuff in the corebook, but were there any particular developments in how Rites were handled in later books that you thought were good or need to be steered away from?<br /> <br /> Just... assessing opinions.<br /> <br /> No reason. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Some rites need to be explicitly more useful. Let's take Bind Spirit, for example. Can a spirit bound Blast outside the circle? (I lean at 'no'; but it's never stated what being bound entails beyond restricted mobility, or how that allows you to have spirits carry on errands for you, once they're not bound again) can I use it like a ward with the specific ban on spirits? No, it only works for an specific one. This is a rank 3 rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T07:14:51-07:00","id":161685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161618#post161618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not, it's a rejection of the premise of your argument - if you don't know how hunting creatures that hide in the souls of people, that you can't see, requires endurance, then you don't know Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Call it what you will; you're still supposed to back it up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T08:13:46-07:00","id":161723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161443#post161443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was more pointing out that Stew promised to change Father Wolf with Mother Wolf, from time to time. Now we see a first draft and all it say's is Father Wolf, no Mother. With this, I started to question is maybe devs changed they mind and stick to old paradigm - which would be far worse. Like I mentioned in previous post - I like idea that I can tweak a bit Uratha culture to local taste and in Scandinavia with it's myths more logical is Mother of Wolves pairing with Father Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>We haven't changed our minds about the Father/Mother flexibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T08:58:02-07:00","id":161785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161685#post161685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Call it what you will; you're still supposed to back it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cop stakeouts require you to stay awake for hours on end, ceaselessly watching and learning details of pattern and behavior in action.<br /> <br /> That's just one example that applies to Storm Lords hunting down the spiritual version of the Unchained. I've got a few more that show how endurance is blatantly needed for this sort of work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T09:34:30-07:00","id":161803,"title":"","content":"What I like most about this write up is the synergy between their Renown, their Ban,and their Prey. Disregarding the fact that a spirit can't help their ban, let's work through this(and I admit, I might not be playing Uratha definitions of words). If all the world were more honorable, there wouldn't be a need a to hide weakness, since people would honorably pit strength against strength, or at least their own weakness against weakness. THe world <i>isn't</i> like that though, and so in order to make it through one must hide their weakness and allow no one to see it, all the while striving to set the example and be the better person. The most abominable thing to such a people, then, would be those who exploited weakness cruelly for their own benefit, and who does that the most? Werewolves, spirits, shartha, and humanity have <i>nothing </i>on those who have Ridden or Claimed people in their moments of weakness and took them for everything in that moment. It's an affront to the ideal, and woe to anyone who thinks they can violate Honor so blatantly. Of course, the danger with dealing with that is that you yourself could be Ridden or Claimed, so the only way to be safe is to never show weakness, at any time.<br /> <br /> Least, that's how I see it. It's a little more noble and idealistic than I think the Storm Lords would see it, but then again there was a time we all wanted to be heroes, and we never let go of those times as easily as we think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T10:11:08-07:00","id":161834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161785#post161785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cop stakeouts require you to stay awake for hours on end, ceaselessly watching and learning details of pattern and behavior in action.<br /> <br /> That's just one example</div> </div> </div> </div>Got any examples that are a challenge for a werewolf's superhuman abilities?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T11:05:48-07:00","id":161871,"title":"","content":"Sure. Take the afore mentioned scenario, and then account that you are not surveilling a human spy but an actual body snatcher.<br /> <br /> This could take a lot more time.<br /> <br /> A Claimed also feasibly has more methods of escape than any other given enemy minus the ability to gnaw through the gauntlet(and do insane routes since they can always get another body), will up a hell of fight since they aren't limited by the moral concerns of what happens to the body(and thus can go full force), and once you catch the bastard and can reasonably do so the best answer is to draw the spirit out of the person and try and fix the damage. The longer a claimed goes, the more damage is done, so it's not like once you start you can actually stop. So that involves crazy long chases through hell and creation,crazy long subudal fights against a creature with nothing to lose, and a long and tiring ritual to tear the thing out of the person.<br /> <br /> As an example.<br /> <br /> The Claimed and Ridden go to extremes in ways werewolves,spirits, sharthas, and humans can't even really fully imagine. It takes endurance on all fronts to withstand those extremes and still be able to 'strike' when it's all over.<br /> <br /> Final note: Most werewolves are not so superhuman that stakeouts are easy for them. Stakeouts aren't actually easy things-it's a challenge to stay alert and attentive for hours on end with doing just the one thing without getting noticed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T11:59:08-07:00","id":161896,"title":"","content":"That looks like a lot of &quot;ifs&quot; to me. Take this bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161871#post161871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Claimed and Ridden go to extremes in ways werewolves,spirits, sharthas, and humans can't even really fully imagine. It takes endurance on all fronts to withstand those extremes and still be able to 'strike' when it's all over.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only true if the Claimed has the abilities to back that emotion. If the werewolf backs it into a corner and the worst it can do is fire a pistol...<br /> <br /> And a long and tiring ritual. That's only true if you're not comfortable with just ending it in a quick swipe of the claws.<br /> <br /> <br /> You're looking at the worst case scenario; the best case scenario is that a Werewolf sees a Claimed, recognises the physical transformation (or has a useful Gift) and ends it in a quick bite.<br /> <br /> And that's the crux of my point. You're not using anything inherent or common the Ridden/Claimed. You're relying on individuals who act in a certain way; but by that logic even Hunters could be an Endurance foe - they have the same exterminate and desperation, their core Risking Willpower mechanic depends on it - and a hidden mastermind who sends minions after the pack could require as much stake outs and investigation as any Claimed. You can make an individual of any splat fit any kind of antagonistic role.<br /> <br /> Compare the Ridden/Claimed to Mask slashers - yes Masks are a bit of a one note, but that one note makes high Stamina mechanically optimum for 1v1 combat. There's no point increasing your damage but you can get a lot of advantages from extra health since that lets you last long enough to gradually wear the Mask down; and of course it feels like Endurance to have a character get stabbed in the gut dozens of times but keep fighting until the Mask falls.<br /> <br /> <br /> But while it's a universal trait to Masks that high Stamina is more useful than high strength, there's no equivalent to Claimed. Nothing common to all of them that makes high Endurance the superior strategy. (And if there was; it's certainly not highlighted in the write up)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T12:04:16-07:00","id":161899,"title":"","content":"If you're just looking for a reason why the Storm Lords go after the Claimed instead of going on this entire endurance kick<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice/page3\">,I already addressed that concern</a>.<br /> <br /> And a Storm Lord who plans for the best case scenario is showing a huge weakness. Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T13:05:30-07:00","id":161947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161443#post161443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was more pointing out that Stew promised to change Father Wolf with Mother Wolf, from time to time. Now we see a first draft and all it say's is Father Wolf, no Mother. With this, I started to question is maybe devs changed they mind and stick to old paradigm - which would be far worse. Like I mentioned in previous post - I like idea that I can tweak a bit Uratha culture to local taste and in Scandinavia with it's myths more logical is Mother of Wolves pairing with Father Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that draft was so full of minor errors (the hunter chased the hunter! round and round they went!), I couldn't stop myself from redlining it myself. It's <i>just a first draft</i>. Don't read anything into the specific words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T13:08:14-07:00","id":161956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161609#post161609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine they'd see Changelings roughly the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I can't agree. There's no tag-along entity accompanying Changelings the way that Geists hitch rides on their Sin Eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T13:11:16-07:00","id":161957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161899#post161899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're just looking for a reason why the Storm Lords go after the Claimed instead of going on this entire endurance kick<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice/page3\">,I already addressed that concern</a>.<br /> <br /> And a Storm Lord who plans for the best case scenario is showing a huge weakness. Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking for a reason why focusing on hunting Ridden/Claimed will lead to a focus on endurance through a cultural/Darwinistic process.<br /> <br /> Or the reverse; a reason why focusing on endurance will lead to a cultural belief that Ridden/Claimed are the most worthy prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T13:15:32-07:00","id":161958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161957#post161957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm looking for a reason why focusing on hunting Ridden/Claimed will lead to a focus on endurance through a cultural/Darwinistic process.<br /> <br /> Or the reverse; a reason why focusing on endurance will lead to a cultural belief that Ridden/Claimed are the most worthy prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>The, uh, fiction? About the Storm Lord laughing off a poisoned wound in the center of a blizzard?<br /> <br /> You got my original argument wrong - the idea isn't to move fast or smartly, it's about weathering the storm so you can analyze the lightning. Ben Franklin and his kite, except in his case the lightning wasn't actively wanting him dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T06:03:35-07:00","id":163489,"title":"","content":"Something I like about the Storm Lords from the player's side of things is that there is such an untenable series of factors you need to meet to attain the 'ideal' situation and be the perfect stereotypical Imnir. You need to be cloaked in ice and cold? That will be tough if your game is set in Florida - except that you can interpret the dogged stamina to withstand the heat as being your way of following Winter Wolf. You need to be the stubborn, prickly one who goes it alone and expects others to follow? That has to be reinterpreted if you are playing pack beta or omega - or if you are playing the team's social wolf? Now you have to interpret moderating your team's emotions and being an effective, maybe even 'friendly' face to the outside. What if you want to be a ranged specialist, or a were which is clearly not in their prime, whether disfigured, injured, too young, too old? An imnir who has a history or who has failed before? Now, for you, showing no weakness is taking pride in withstanding the disappointment of others, being true to yourself despite others' ignorance of what it *really* means to be Imnir. In short, because not every game is going to make you play a cookie cutter, five dots in stamina composure resolve whatever, there is an enormous space for personal drama and struggle and horror in the wheelhouse of 'being at the top of my game' for the Imnir. Just my two cents, thought it might be helpful to the posters who keep asking about being pigeonholed into 'hunting ridden' or 'being cold' and feeling hobbled: if you feel bothered by that, it should be a clear message to your ST to help you see a more flexible and uncertain world that you can be a little different in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":".  spacing 06-09-2014, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:11:53-07:00","id":163639,"title":"","content":"My thinks some people are mistaking a footprint(symbol) for a boot(idea).<br /> <br /> The Storm Lords prefer to cloak themselves in their chosen metaphor, but they don't <i>need</i> winter-esque things. It's just the most pertinent way to make the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:46:27-07:00","id":163698,"title":"","content":"Agreed. These are werewolves, not superheroes. They don't need a Winter Wolf-mobile and an Iminir-cave and a Storm Lords-wing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">((although, retreating to the Iminir Cave sounds kinda cool))</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:54:46-07:00","id":163710,"title":"","content":"Eh, in the writers' defense, some symbols get pretty evocative. A spirit quest in a walk-in freezer is a pretty skewing image as far as making unseasonable heat into kryptonite for a character's identity. ...not saying readers shouldn't read critically and practice a little creativity, but there's a little bit of ode, homage, or fan-ficcing celebration of others' ideas in all p&amp;p - otherwise creative property wouldn't be valuable and tropes wouldn't be useful shorthand to get your story across the table. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T10:08:12-07:00","id":163727,"title":"","content":"Seems like they should be called Winter Wolves, if they're so big on cold. I get the weather the Storm Lord thing, though having lived in a tropical climate a vast majority of my life I view storms as more wet, often even steamy than cold.<br /> <br /> I imagine tests of endurance would be more along the lines of wearing your black suit and black pants and tie and jacket and standing out on the seven mile bridge during the day, occasionally slipping your glasses on or off to make quips.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T10:24:18-07:00","id":163785,"title":"","content":"That idea would 'suit' me as *glasses* Right as rain. YEAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAH","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T10:41:04-07:00","id":163799,"title":"","content":"There's already a Winter Wolf in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T11:08:12-07:00","id":163811,"title":"","content":"Yes, Skolis-Ur, the firstborn totem of the Storm Lords is the Winter Wolf, but if they were more about cold, it may make more sense to call them Winter Wolves than Storm Lords. Though obviously as ArcaneArts put it, footprint, boot.<br /> <br /> Since these are just names, changing Winter Wolf to Storm Wolf isn't a drastic change that would alter the game entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:46:18-07:00","id":163913,"title":"","content":"There are a few examples of the Storm Lords braving storms as rites of passage. I think lodge of the maelstrom has you sitting on the beach no matter the weather. One of their major lodges came about from them standing in a storm (in i want to say ancient middle east) and essentially giving the storm the finger. <br /> <br /> It's not always about the cold, but Skolis-Ur being WINTER wolf, his domain is usually frigid. Endurance is important per the defiance aspect as well. Not sure why that was ever a question... and some claimed can give you a pretty good run for your money if they've been claimed long enough. Look at the Alder Man from Mantiou Springs (AKA Werewolf the Forsaken demo).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:59:14-07:00","id":163925,"title":"","content":"I only will nitpick this Bankok - wouldn't be it more suitable if they would try to withstand monsoons or tornadoes? I know the follow <b><i>Winter </i>Wolf</b>, but they are <b><i>Storm </i>Lords</b>, don't they? And what about Australia - they try to use refrigerators in center of bush? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:09:15-07:00","id":163936,"title":"","content":"That is kind of what I was saying before. It would look less blurry if you weren't staring so hard: nothing is perfect in the WoD, not even the myths. It just shouldn't be such a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:12:07-07:00","id":163938,"title":"","content":"Heat and dehydration in the bush.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:42:13-07:00","id":163964,"title":"","content":"The idea is that a storm is one of the most intensive things to endure by yourself. TO be fair, a blizzard is one of the harshest storms a person can live through(not disparaging monsoons and hurricanes, but still), and therefore one of the strongest images to enact and incorporate into your culture(plus Skolis himself). Ice itself also lends to the Storm Lords mentality-it can be hard, it can be sharp, it can be soft, ever present, and dismissable, it can help spread light(hope and encouragement) to others or it can block it out, and of course, it's most insisidous and enduring fact is that all other facts aside, the cold will slowly grip you, and the longer that game goes on, the worse most things do against it-regardless of how that ice manifests. Plus, as a minor nod of Storm Lords to the Iron Masters as shared philosophies go, ice can always change into water and take on new things. It's pervasive in it's effects.<br /> <br /> That said, I grew up in the desert. Power was a brown out, a sheet of lightning dancing across the flats, a sun that refused to look away and dared clouds to cross it's gaze(few did). All of those are quite evocative of the Storm Lords, because they <i>endure the storm</i>.<br /> <br /> A Blizzard may be the most potent of images to the Lords, going all the way to the heat death of the universe as the ultimately conquest of cold, but storms of any kind serve the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T21:52:10-07:00","id":164477,"title":"","content":"You know, these discussions sound pretty close to what I'd expect an international gathering of Iminir to sound like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T02:33:57-07:00","id":164677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161609#post161609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I imagine they'd see Changelings roughly the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Bangkok, where the average temperature rarely dips below 70\u00b0<br /> <br /> Fahrenheit, Iminir lock themselves in refrigerated trucks for hours at a time, hoping<br /> <br /> that Skolis-Ur will favor them with visions of their prey\u2019s weakness. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey Jimmy Jock! you know that wolfy looking dude that nearly tore that spring prince a new one? Well, the dude's passed out in the freezer and I got the the Autumn court on the line. I'll see if I can pull a favor out of spring return for putting one in for Autumn. With any luck, we should have a Scarecrow give him some good ol' dose of their best Nightmare Fuel!&quot; <br /> <br /> Word to the wise, don't screw with people who plant and harvest Nightmare Fuel on a regular basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T07:32:33-07:00","id":164821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=164477#post164477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, these discussions sound pretty close to what I'd expect an international gathering of Iminir to sound like.</div> </div> </div> </div>As it should be.....which is why they usually don't meet on an international scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T08:02:29-07:00","id":164835,"title":"","content":"&quot;Mister Speaker, would you please tell the delegate from Brazil to kiss my desh kar?&quot; &quot;Sigh....we will have a ten minute recess for another trial of honor. Everyone clear the floor.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T13:27:11-07:00","id":165087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=163964#post163964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea is that a storm is one of the most intensive things to endure by yourself. TO be fair, a blizzard is one of the harshest storms a person can live through(not disparaging monsoons and hurricanes, but still), and therefore one of the strongest images to enact and incorporate into your culture(plus Skolis himself). Ice itself also lends to the Storm Lords mentality-it can be hard, it can be sharp, it can be soft, ever present, and dismissable, it can help spread light(hope and encouragement) to others or it can block it out, and of course, it's most insisidous and enduring fact is that all other facts aside, the cold will slowly grip you, and the longer that game goes on, the worse most things do against it-regardless of how that ice manifests. Plus, as a minor nod of Storm Lords to the Iron Masters as shared philosophies go, ice can always change into water and take on new things. It's pervasive in it's effects.<br /> <br /> That said, I grew up in the desert. Power was a brown out, a sheet of lightning dancing across the flats, a sun that refused to look away and dared clouds to cross it's gaze(few did). All of those are quite evocative of the Storm Lords, because they <i>endure the storm</i>.<br /> <br /> A Blizzard may be the most potent of images to the Lords, going all the way to the heat death of the universe as the ultimately conquest of cold, but storms of any kind serve the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still don't change that Strom Lords in Bankok should be putting themselves against hurricanes, not refrigerators. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:01:37-07:00","id":165138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=165087#post165087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still don't change that Strom Lords in Bankok should be putting themselves against hurricanes, not refrigerators. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><i>The ocean called, they're all out of hurricanes.</i><br /> <br /> But seriously, a refrigerator is something everyone can get access to. Cyclones have a specific season and may not even hit Bangkok. More often than not they pass by and cause flooding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-10-2014, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:14:12-07:00","id":165145,"title":"","content":"Why not do both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:37:44-07:00","id":165207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=165145#post165145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not do both?</div> </div> </div> </div> A vision quest in an commercial refrigerator in a cyclone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T15:02:27-07:00","id":165241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=165207#post165207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A vision quest in an commercial refrigerator in a cyclone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or when a cyclone's comin you get out there, but the rest of the year you have your fridges and other tortures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-10-2014, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T15:17:10-07:00","id":165280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=165207#post165207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A vision quest in an commercial refrigerator in a cyclone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, if you can't have a vision in a fridge in a hurricane, there's no hope for you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T00:54:48-07:00","id":165711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=165138#post165138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>The ocean called, they're all out of hurricanes.</i><br /> <br /> But seriously, a refrigerator is something everyone can get access to. Cyclones have a specific season and may not even hit Bangkok. More often than not they pass by and cause flooding.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It still makes no sense on a cultural basis for Bangkok Storm Lords (or Storm Lords from anywhere tropical) to view the cold as the 'ultimate endurance'. If we take winter to mean 'the harshest time of the year', then that's most likely the rain season of Thailand, so they'd probably do near-drownings. Winter =/= cold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T04:52:28-07:00","id":165800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=165711#post165711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still makes no sense on a cultural basis for Bangkok Storm Lords (or Storm Lords from anywhere tropical) to view the cold as the 'ultimate endurance'. <b>If we take winter to mean 'the harshest time of the year',</b> then that's most likely the rain season of Thailand, so they'd probably do near-drownings. Winter =/= cold.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this explanation. It made me realize how euro-centric the &quot;official&quot; story of the Winter Wolf is (what with the world becoming cold and all) and where my cultural bias was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T04:56:17-07:00","id":165805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=165711#post165711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still makes no sense on a cultural basis for Bangkok Storm Lords (or Storm Lords from anywhere tropical) to view the cold as the 'ultimate endurance'. If we take winter to mean 'the harshest time of the year', then that's most likely the rain season of Thailand, so they'd probably do near-drownings. Winter =/= cold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I pointed out in post #49.<br /> But I'd also point out that just like there's not always cyclones, it's not always the rainy season.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T16:19:24-07:00","id":166319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=165800#post165800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like this explanation. It made me realize how euro-centric the &quot;official&quot; story of the Winter Wolf is (what with the world becoming cold and all) and where my cultural bias was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ice Ages are whole world affairs. Just sayin'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T16:58:03-07:00","id":166344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=166319#post166319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ice Ages are whole world affairs. Just sayin'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, there's nothing &quot;Euro&quot; about the Himalayas or the Andes. Contrary to what the Sheriff's Secret Police would have you believe, mountains are in fact real and the taller ones are often quite cold.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the nearest major mountainous region to Bangkok is in Northern Thailand, and Bangkok is on the southern edge of Central, so cold-trucks are still more convenient.<br /> <br /> This is to say nothing of how assuming harsh climate is what Winter Wolf's motif is built on ignores the existence of deserts as an entire symbolset that's clearly out of theme for that particular Firstborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-11-2014, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T22:50:33-07:00","id":166646,"title":"","content":"The problem with harsh climates of other kinds lies in the other Firstborn(or potential ones) also touching on them. The desert and heat would tie more into Rabid Wolf and the Fire-touched. Less with an elemental focus, but more with the idea of their conviction and faith burning away heretics and the unworthy. Much like Skolis-Ur and the Storm Lords are less about summoning up ice and more about enduring hardship. So while being in the middle of a storm of any variety works for Storm Lord trials, I think its more of a motif thing since cold would work well with Winter Wolf. Just like the Fire-Touched like to play with fire in their trials.<br /> <br /> Also, a potential Sea Wolf for another Tribe would like to have some room to play in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T14:13:27-07:00","id":167220,"title":"","content":"Regarding ideas about Rites, I think that something like Machine IV's Kigan system would be really cool. I like the idea of being able to create effects by leveraging a spirit's Influences rather than creating the effect yourself, but I'm not sure if that should be a Gift or a Rite or something else...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T14:54:29-07:00","id":167237,"title":"","content":"I imagine before the refrigerator was invented those Storm Lords living in Bangkok had localized rituals and cultures...and still do, but with the advent of technology they see a way to get a little closer to the spiritual essence of their tribal totem. I do think it's a bit silly and could use some expansion to include other forms of stormy weather (with an emphasis on storm), but I think when the option is available any Storm Lord would prefer to find somewhere cold to channel Winter Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}